.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt NVSO 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvso
.Nd research driver for soft SO domains and SSD DMA bookkeeping
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd device nvso
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes a character device
.Pa /dev/nvso0
and an ioctl ABI for creating isolated compute domains, mapping address
ranges (including NVM-backed regions), exporting SSD queue geometry, and
posting GPU DMA descriptor lists.
.Pp
This is a
.Em research
driver with a
.Em soft
HVVRAM domain path (ABI 2): domain create/map/gate/irq and soft queue
export / DMA post succeed as in-kernel bookkeeping only.
Stock NVIDIA G84 silicon does not implement independent SO clock domains
as described in the design thread; open SandForce firmware is not included.
Real SSD/GPU DMA is
.Em not
implemented.
.Sh IOCTLS
Defined in
.In nvso_ioctl.h
(group
.Ql N ) :
.Bl -tag -width "NVSSD_QUEUE_EXPORTXX"
.It Dv NVSO_DOMAIN_CREATE
Create a domain.
Userspace name alias:
.Fn nvso_domain_create .
.It Dv NVSO_MAP
Map a VA range into a domain.
Alias:
.Fn nvso_map .
.It Dv NVSSD_QUEUE_EXPORT
Export raw SSD queue geometry into a domain.
Alias:
.Fn nvssd_queue_export .
.It Dv NVGPU_DMA_POST
Post a DMA descriptor array (GPU/SSD/peer).
Alias:
.Fn nvgpu_dma_post .
.It Dv NVSO_DOMAIN_GATE
Power-gate or ungate a domain.
Alias:
.Fn nvso_domain_gate .
.It Dv NVSO_IRQ_ATTACH
Attach a domain-local notification.
Alias:
.Fn nvso_irq_attach .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/nvso0"
.It Pa /dev/nvso0
Control device node.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvso 9 ,
.Xr ioctl 2
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
stub first appeared in the familia
.Pa gpu-legacy/nvso
tree (2026-10-26).
.Sh BUGS
Soft bookkeeping only; no hardware SSD/GPU DMA. Loading is for ABI bring-up only.
